  "label": "Black people are mapped onto the woman holding the artifact",
  "description": "The text 'black people' is overlaid directly above the woman's head, visually mapping the textual label 'black people' onto the visual entity 'woman'. This creates an analogical mapping where the woman is being identified or represented as 'black people', despite her visual appearance (light brown hair, etc.). This mapping is central to the meme's hateful message, as it uses the visual of the woman holding the artifact to reinforce the racist trope that Black people are not entitled to cultural artifacts.",
